+# Penny & Microcap Shadow Scanner — Telegram Bot Setup
+
+Fourth route in the per-scanner pattern in `TELEGRAM_THREE_BOT_ROUTING.md`. Work
+through the steps in order; steps 1–6 are done in Telegram and GitHub, steps 7–9
+are in the repository. Nothing is delivered until step 8 passes.
+
+**Never put a token or chat ID in a source file, a workflow file, or a commit.**
+All values are GitHub Actions secrets.
+
+---
+
+## Step 1 — Create the bot
+
+In Telegram, message **@BotFather**:
+
+```
+/newbot
+```
+
+- **Name** (display name): `NSE Penny Shadow`
+- **Username** (must end in `bot`): e.g. `nse_penny_shadow_bot`
+
+BotFather replies with an HTTP API token shaped like
+`8123456789:AAH...`. Copy it once; it is `PENNY_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN`.
+
+Recommended hardening, still in @BotFather:
+
+```
+/setjoingroups   → Enable   (the bot must join your group)
+/setprivacy      → Disable  (lets the bot read commands in the group; skip if
+                             you only ever push and never issue commands)
+/setdescription  → Penny & microcap paper research. Not trading advice.
+/setcommands     → status - delivery and gateway status
+                   radar - today's early radar list
+                   ready - entry-authorised candidates
+```
+
+> `/setcommands` only matters if you later add a polling handler. Delivery-only
+> operation needs no commands.
+
+---
+
+## Step 2 — Create the group and enable topics
+
+1. Create a **new group** — do not reuse the V3, Ladder or Hull group. Isolation
+   is the point: a penny card must never land in a large-cap topic.
+2. Name it e.g. `NSE Penny Shadow — Paper`.
+3. Add your new bot as a **member**, then promote it to **admin**. A bot cannot
+   post into topics without admin rights.
+4. Group settings → **Topics** → **Enable**.
+
+---
+
+## Step 3 — Create the four delivery topics
+
+Create these topics in the group. The split lets you mute the radar firehose
+without losing entry authorisations:
+
+| Topic | Holds |
+|---|---|
+| `Early Radar` | movement starting; observation only |
+| `Confirming` | participation confirming; still not an entry |
+| `Ready` | entry-authorised paper candidates |
+| `Circuit Risk` | circuit-locked, extended, terminal |
+| `Portfolio` | paper positions and reconciliation |
+| `System` | daily summary, gateway diagnostics, failures |
+
+---
+
+## Step 4 — Find the chat ID and topic IDs
+
+**Chat ID.** Post any message in the group, then open:
+
+```
+https://api.telegram.org/bot<YOUR_TOKEN>/getUpdates
+```
+
+Look for `"chat":{"id":-1001234567890,...}`. Supergroup IDs are negative and
+start `-100`. That is `PENNY_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID`.
+
+**Topic IDs.** In Telegram Desktop, right-click a topic → **Copy Link**. You get
+`https://t.me/c/1234567890/57` — the trailing number (`57`) is the topic ID. In
+`getUpdates` the same value appears as `message_thread_id`.
+
+> If `getUpdates` returns an empty `result`, post a fresh message and retry. If a
+> webhook is set the endpoint stays empty; call `/deleteWebhook` first.
+
+---
+
+## Step 5 — Add the GitHub Actions secrets
+
+Repository → **Settings** → **Secrets and variables** → **Actions** → **New
+repository secret**.
+
+**Required** — delivery fails closed without both:
+
+| Secret | Value |
+|---|---|
+| `PENNY_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` | the @BotFather token |
+| `PENNY_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID` | e.g. `-1001234567890` |
+
+**Optional** — omit any and that section posts to the chat root:
+
+| Secret | Value |
+|---|---|
+| `PENNY_RADAR_TOPIC_ID` | topic ID for `Early Radar` |
+| `PENNY_CONFIRMING_TOPIC_ID` | topic ID for `Confirming` |
+| `PENNY_READY_TOPIC_ID` | topic ID for `Ready` |
+| `PENNY_CIRCUIT_TOPIC_ID` | topic ID for `Circuit Risk` |
+| `PENNY_PORTFOLIO_TOPIC_ID` | topic ID for `Portfolio` |
+| `PENNY_SYSTEM_TOPIC_ID` | topic ID for `System` |
+
+---
+
+## Step 6 — Confirm the bot can post
+
+Before involving the repository, prove the credentials work:
+
+```bash
+curl -s "https://api.telegram.org/bot<TOKEN>/sendMessage" \
+  -d chat_id="-1001234567890" \
+  -d message_thread_id="57" \
+  -d text="penny route check"
+```
+
+`{"ok":true,...}` means the bot is a group admin and the topic ID is valid.
+
+Common failures:
+
+| Response | Cause |
+|---|---|
+| `403 bot is not a member of the group` | bot not added |
+| `400 not enough rights to send text messages` | bot not admin |
+| `400 message thread not found` | wrong topic ID, or topics disabled |
+| `400 chat not found` | chat ID missing the `-100` prefix |
+
+---
+
+## Step 7 — Local smoke test
+
+Renders the real card format and reports which secrets are visible, without
+printing any of their values:
+
+```bash
+# see what the environment exposes; sends nothing
+python scripts/penny_telegram_smoke.py
+
+# preview one section's cards
+python scripts/penny_telegram_smoke.py --section radar
+
+# actually deliver sample cards to every configured topic
+export PENNY_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=...
+export PENNY_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=-1001234567890
+export PENNY_RADAR_TOPIC_ID=57
+python scripts/penny_telegram_smoke.py --send
+```
+
+Expected on success: `All configured routes delivered. Safe to wire the scanner.`
+
+---
+
+## Step 8 — Wire the scanner
+
+`penny_shadow/cards.py` renders from plain dictionaries, so it does not care how
+the scanner is structured internally. Each candidate needs `symbol` and `score`;
+every other field degrades to `Not yet confirmed` rather than rendering a
+misleading zero.
+
+```python
+from penny_shadow.cards import render_sections, render_summary
+from penny_shadow.telegram import (
+    send_radar, send_confirming, send_ready, send_circuit, send_system,
+)
+
+# candidates: list of dicts from the penny scanner
+#   symbol, score, cmp, return_5d, turnover_ratio, delivery_pct, trend,
+#   stage         -> RADAR | CONFIRMING | QUALIFIED | READY
+#   availability  -> CIRCUIT_LOCKED | CIRCUIT_WATCH | EXTENDED | TERMINATED | None
+#   market_cap_verified -> False marks the card observation-only
+#   entry_low / entry_high / stop, notes[]
+
+messages = render_sections(candidates, market_date)
+send_radar([messages["radar"]], enabled=live) if "radar" in messages else None
+send_confirming([messages["confirming"]], enabled=live) if "confirming" in messages else None
+send_ready([messages["ready"]], enabled=live) if "ready" in messages else None
+send_circuit([messages["circuit"]], enabled=live) if "circuit" in messages else None
+send_system(render_summary(candidates, market_date, gateway=verdict.diagnostics()),
+            enabled=live)
+```
+
+Set `stage` from the shared vocabulary in `v2/progressive_stages.py`, and
+`availability` from `availability_from_gateway(...)` so the gateway's decisions
+reach the card. A symbol whose `availability` is a circuit or terminal state is
+routed to **Circuit Risk** and never to **Ready**, whatever it scored — that is
+how NHCFOODS stays detected while remaining unbuyable.
+
+### Apply the shared gateway too
+
+The penny scanner should run the same admission control as the other three:
+
+```python
+from v2.tradeability import gateway_from_database
+
+verdict = gateway_from_database(db_path, prices)
+prices = verdict.filter_frame(prices)
+# entry authorisation additionally requires verdict.entry_permitted(symbol)
+```
+
+Penny-specific note: at `EARLY RADAR` the specification allows an unverified
+market cap. Pass `require_universe_membership=False` (the default) so such a
+symbol is admitted and labelled `NON_EQ_UNVERIFIED` / observe-only, rather than
+rejected — and set `market_cap_verified=False` on the card so it reads
+`UNVERIFIED — observation only`.
+
+---
+
+## Step 9 — Schedule it
+
+Add a workflow mirroring `.github/workflows/pine-hull-daily.yml`, passing only
+the `PENNY_*` secrets:
+
+```yaml
+    env:
+      PYTHONPATH: ${{ github.workspace }}
+      PENNY_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.PENNY_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN }}
+      PENNY_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID: ${{ secrets.PENNY_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID }}
+      PENNY_RADAR_TOPIC_ID: ${{ secrets.PENNY_RADAR_TOPIC_ID }}
+      PENNY_CONFIRMING_TOPIC_ID: ${{ secrets.PENNY_CONFIRMING_TOPIC_ID }}
+      PENNY_READY_TOPIC_ID: ${{ secrets.PENNY_READY_TOPIC_ID }}
+      PENNY_CIRCUIT_TOPIC_ID: ${{ secrets.PENNY_CIRCUIT_TOPIC_ID }}
+      PENNY_PORTFOLIO_TOPIC_ID: ${{ secrets.PENNY_PORTFOLIO_TOPIC_ID }}
+      PENNY_SYSTEM_TOPIC_ID: ${{ secrets.PENNY_SYSTEM_TOPIC_ID }}
+```
+
+Do **not** expose `V3_*`, `LADDER_*` or `HULL_*` secrets to this job. The route
+is isolated by construction, and a test asserts it cannot borrow another
+scanner's bot.
+
+Run for at least a week with `--send` disabled, compare the rendered previews
+against the scanner's own output, then enable live delivery.
+
+---
+
+## Operating notes
+
+- **Fail closed.** A missing `PENNY_*` credential returns
+  `penny_telegram_credentials_missing` and delivers nothing. It never falls back
+  to another bot.
+- **Long lists.** Messages over 4,096 characters split on card boundaries, so a
+  card is never truncated mid-way.
+- **Rotating the token.** `/revoke` in @BotFather, then update the secret. The
+  chat and topic IDs are unaffected.
+- **Rate limits.** Roughly 20 messages/minute per group. Delivery sleeps 1s
+  between messages; prefer one message per section over one per stock.
